{"is_source_file": true, "format": "Python", "description": "This file defines various dropout classes in PyTorch's neural network modules, including Dropout, Dropout1d, Dropout2d, Dropout3d, AlphaDropout, and FeatureAlphaDropout. It also includes an internal base class '_DropoutNd' that they inherit from. The classes provide various forms of dropout regularization techniques used during neural network training.", "external_files": ["torch.nn.functional", "torch"], "external_methods": ["F.dropout", "F.dropout1d", "F.dropout2d", "F.dropout3d", "F.alpha_dropout", "F.feature_alpha_dropout"], "published": ["Dropout", "Dropout1d", "Dropout2d", "Dropout3d", "AlphaDropout", "FeatureAlphaDropout"], "classes": [{"name": "_DropoutNd", "description": "An internal base class for various dropout layers, encapsulating common attributes like probability 'p' and 'inplace', as well as constants.", "methods": [{"name": "extra_repr", "description": "Returns a string representation of the dropout's parameters."}]}, {"name": "Dropout", "description": "Implements the standard dropout that randomly zeroes individual elements of the input tensor during training, scaling the outputs accordingly.", "methods": [{"name": "forward", "description": "Applies dropout to the input tensor during training phase."}]}, {"name": "Dropout1d", "description": "Zeroes out entire channels of 1D feature maps, effective for regularizing convolutional outputs with 1D spatial dimensions.", "methods": [{"name": "forward", "description": "Applies 1D feature map dropout during the forward pass."}]}, {"name": "Dropout2d", "description": "Zeroes out entire channels of 2D feature maps, typically used after convolutional layers dealing with image data.", "methods": [{"name": "forward", "description": "Applies 2D feature map dropout during the forward pass."}]}, {"name": "Dropout3d", "description": "Zeroes out entire channels of 3D feature maps, used for volumetric data such as videos or 3D images.", "methods": [{"name"